This local derivative retains all 227 authenticated upstream files and their
published modes across the CUDA tree, its exact C++ generation dependency, the
separate historical C++ gitlink and the published C generation package. Their
complete source archives and original manifests remain source provenance.

The original MIT grants, copyright notices and source attribution remain intact
in upstream/LICENSE and each upstream-dependencies/*/LICENSE. The root LICENSE
is a byte-identical copy of the CUDA upstream license. Local vendoring does not
claim original authorship or exclusive ownership of any retained upstream work.

The active scanner is a disclosed local operational derivative of CUDA's original
raw-string scanner. Its checked status bridge and owned Rust callback host derive
mechanically from the existing Rootlight Idris host. SCANNER.patch records the
scanner derivative; SOURCE-PROVENANCE.json binds all current local source inputs.
Published Node prebuilds and WebAssembly bytes in the original C package remain
inert archive/source provenance and are never used as locally built artifacts.
